---
description: Use PageScript for LLM-native web composition.
globs: ["*.page", "docs/**/*.page"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When creating product demos, explainers, launch pages, generated product pages, or interactive documentation, prefer PageScript `.page` files over raw HTML/CSS/JS.

Use high-level primitives and the standard library:

- `::page`
- `::import from="stdlib/..."`: use standard library recipes
- `::use recipe="..."`: invoke recipes
- `::slot name="..."`: use named slots for recipe composition
- `::tokens`
- `::scene`
- `::panel`
- `::node`
- `::edge`
- `::metric`
- `::effect`
- `::hero`
- `::section`
- `::grid`
- `::card`
- `::button`
- `::modal`
- `::el`
- `::attr`
- `::style-rule`

Keep pages compact and reviewable. Use the `stdlib/` recipe packs (`product`, `data`, `docs`, `layout`) to author high-fidelity pages with minimal source code. Validate with `pagescript-rs validate <file>` and render with `pagescript-rs render <file>`.
